# A1 moves from "sensible qualities" to "intelligible qualities". These are different words for qualities, not one word in two senses. In the text, the primary qualities count as sensible too, so A1 joins two different claims and is not a bridge.
# "contrary to reason" means "in conflict with what reason shows" in S1 and in S2 alike. The second objection only presses it further, so I count it as one sense.
